WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.013
A square tile has an area of twelve square units. Its side is the square root of twelve. That is a surd: a root that is not a whole number. Exact means we keep the root, not a calculator decimal.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:25.272
To simplify a surd, take out a square number. Twelve is four times three, and the root of four is two. So root twelve is two root three.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:39.815
The denominator is the bottom of a fraction. To rationalise means to remove the surd from the bottom. Multiply top and bottom by the same number. One over root five becomes root five over five.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:51.931
If the bottom has two terms, use its conjugate: the same terms with the sign between them changed. Multiply them and the surd vanishes: twenty minus one is nineteen.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:01:02.657
These questions give a fraction and ask for a and b in the form a plus b root c. You rationalise, simplify, then compare.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:18.572
Step one: put the surd fraction on its own. If a side comes from an area, divide the area by the known length. Step two: multiply top and bottom by the conjugate of the bottom.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:34.420
Step three: expand the top term by term. Step four: collect whole numbers and surds, and divide. Step five: compare with the form. The trap: two root five squared is twenty, not ten.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:52.609
November twenty twenty three. A right-angled triangle has sides two plus four root five, and a plus b root five. Its area is thirty four plus eleven root five. Find a and b without a calculator. Four marks.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:04.647
Step one: the area is a half times the two short sides. Half of two plus four root five is one plus two root five. So that times a plus b root five equals the area.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:17.018
Step two: divide, then multiply top and bottom by the conjugate. Write the bottom as two root five plus one. Its conjugate is two root five minus one.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:26.466
A tempting wrong route is multiplying by the bottom itself. The bottom becomes twenty one plus four root five. The surd is still there.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:39.772
Step three: the top. Thirty four times two root five is sixty eight root five. Then minus thirty four. Then one hundred and ten. Then minus eleven root five.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:50.505
Step four: the bottom is twenty minus one, so nineteen. Divide: four plus three root five. So a is four and b is three.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:57.589
That is exact, with no calculator. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:08.032
A common mistake is squaring three root three as nine root three. Square the three too: nine times three is twenty seven.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:21.804
Now you try, from June twenty twenty two. Write the fraction as a plus b root three, without a calculator. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:33.799
The bottom is three root three plus five. Its conjugate is three root three minus five. Multiply top and bottom by it.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:41.990
Top: eighteen, minus ten root three, minus twelve root three, plus twenty. That is thirty eight minus twenty two root three.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:52.378
Bottom: twenty seven minus twenty five is two. Divide by two: nineteen minus eleven root three. So a is nineteen and b is minus eleven.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:59.463
The most common wrong answer squares three root three as nine root three. Square the three too.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.242
Remember: conjugate, expand, simplify, compare.
